{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Behold, a people like a lioness rises.</b> A hint that he will defeat the kings of Canaan, and that which is close to reason is the nearby thing, like the war against Midian, of which no war like it was heard: not one of the seed of Israel was missing, and five kings died, and human beings who did not know the lying of a male were thirty-two thousand." "<b>And the blood of the slain.</b> The spoil, (as in) 'and all their army' [Numbers 31:11]. And by way of derash: Moses will not lie down until he eats prey — so it is written: 'afterward you will be gathered to your people' [Numbers 31:2]."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Resolved הדבר הקרוב as 'the nearby thing' referring elliptically to the nearby war (Midian); the syntax is compressed and the antecedent implicit.", 1 "The lemma המלקוח is apparently drawn from Numbers 31:11 (ואת כל מלקוחם), here linked to ואת כל חילם of the same verse."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:14.756857067Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}